              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Momof2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We loved, Loved, LOVED these. This is a favorite of ours when we go out to restaurants and I really am glad that I \"finally\" found a recipe that is what we order out. Definate keeper. Thanks for the post."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "R Chase"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I made a few changes to the recipe. I used a Saison beer instead of water, 1 tsp garlic galore, 1 tsp absoutely onion blend and 3/4 tsp season salt. I fried them in a cast iron pan, drained them on a cookie sheet with (paper towel umder it, not on it) and they came out perfectly crisp!",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-19T21:43:25.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lafayette Roe"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Like many others, added my own combination of spices. Mostly Cayenne, white pepper and chili powder. It also helps the crispness to put the batter in the freezer for about 30 minutes while the oil is heating. (Tempura batter trick)",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-27T16:26:10.943Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "carrol cofer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had some baby portebella mushrooms to use &amp; found this batter. I did change it slightly &amp; used beer instead of water. The carbonation made the batter especially light. One could also use seltzer water for the same end result. Since the batter was more than needed for the mushrooms, I sliced some Vidalia onions &amp; used it up. It was bar food at home. Thanks for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-03T12:25:50.590Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "maryann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good, but does need more spice. Also used a deep fryer and fried until brown and crisp. Here is a dip I made: 1/4 cup mayo, 1 tblsp each lemon juice, horseradish, milk to desired consistency. Similar to dips we have tasted served with this dish. Will make this again with some cayenne and more garlic.",
            "datePublished": "2008-07-21T18:55:58.270Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tom C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "First time I made these we didn't like the batter- too mushy. So the next time we dipped the mushrooms in beat egg and the rolled them in italian breadcrumbs (already has garlic and spices added in). They turned out wonderful- crunchy and tasty. Dipped in Hidden Valley Ranch Dressing.",
            "datePublished": "2008-11-02T01:03:59.020Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HPrice0823"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious!! Light, super crispy crust that’s not too thick! You can still taste the mushroom! Prep was easy! We added a few more seasonings: seasoned salt, garlic powder instead of garlic salt, onion powder, pepper, and regular salt. Everyone said they were better than any restaurant mushrooms. Definitely recommend!",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-18T00:40:29.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’ve been looking for something as crunchy as this! I tweaked it a bit with Cajun spices, but followed it to a tee otherwise. Oh, and I also used self rising flour instead of all purpose, because it has baking powder in it which I’ve read also helps makes a crunchier batter. This is great and I will definitely use this recipe again!! Thanks for sharing!☺️",
            "datePublished": "2023-06-04T10:52:51.457Z"
          },
          {
